WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.395 --> 00:00:16.036
stared at the stranger in surprise.

2
00:00:16.056 --> 00:00:20.258
"Yes, we're The Lemonade Detectives," he told him.

3
00:00:20.278 --> 00:00:24.320
"What do you mean, your ice-cream flavor was stolen?"

4
00:00:25.441 --> 00:00:26.682
"I mean someone stole it!"

5
00:00:27.042 --> 00:00:28.723
the man exclaimed with a scowl.

6
00:00:29.403 --> 00:00:30.224
Then he sighed.

7
00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:35.839
"Sorry, I didn't mean to snap at you," he said in a calmer voice.

8
00:00:35.859 --> 00:00:37.480
"I'm just upset."

9
00:00:38.441 --> 00:00:40.382
"Maybe we can help," Maggie said.

10
00:00:40.402 --> 00:00:42.263
"Tell us more about the case."

11
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:43.924
"My name is Mr.

12
00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:48.088
Tate. I'm getting ready to open a new business called the Dessert Den."

13
00:00:48.108 --> 00:00:49.909
"The Dessert Den?"

14
00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:51.470
Cole licked his lips.

15
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.371
"Sounds delicious!"

16
00:00:54.632 --> 00:00:55.913
Henry thought the name of Mr.

17
00:00:55.933 --> 00:00:57.574
Tate's business sounded familiar.

18
00:00:58.455 --> 00:00:59.496
Then he remembered why.

19
00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:03.114
"The Dessert Den is in West Belltown, right?"

20
00:01:03.415 --> 00:01:03.975
he asked.

21
00:01:05.036 --> 00:01:05.897
Mr. Tate nodded.

22
00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:06.777
"That's right."

23
00:01:07.798 --> 00:01:08.739
"How did you know that?"

24
00:01:09.039 --> 00:01:10.060
Maggie asked Henry.

25
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.805
"My dad has been writing a series of stories about that part of town," Henry said.

26
00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:21.049
"There was a bad fire there a long time ago, and the neighborhood got run down.

27
00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:26.253
Now the town council wants to fix up the area and help new businesses open up."

28
00:01:26.273 --> 00:01:29.096
"I know where you mean," Cole said.

29
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.462
"A lot of West Belltown is just empty lots now.

30
00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.924
Some guys from my soccer team live there."

31
00:01:36.205 --> 00:01:36.926
Henry nodded.

32
00:01:36.946 --> 00:01:42.010
"Dad says the people who live in West Belltown have been using the empty lots for all sorts

33
00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:42.470
of things.

34
00:01:43.611 --> 00:01:48.055
They hold neighborhood barbecues there and play soccer and kickball, stuff like that."

35
00:01:49.036 --> 00:01:51.638
Mr. Tate cleared his throat loudly, looking impatient.

36
00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:54.280
"You kids are younger than I expected.

37
00:01:54.961 --> 00:01:55.982
Are you really detectives?"

38
00:01:57.343 --> 00:01:58.664
"Yes," Maggie said.

39
00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:00.897
"We've solved lots of mysteries.

40
00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:05.739
If anyone in Belltown can solve your case, it's The Lemonade Detectives!"

41
00:02:06.719 --> 00:02:08.140
"Okay." Mr.

42
00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.440
Tate still looked uncertain.

43
00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.041
"But I need this problem solved quickly.

44
00:02:12.741 --> 00:02:14.982
The Dessert Den's grand opening is this Friday."

45
00:02:15.002 --> 00:02:17.623
"Friday?" Cole cried.

46
00:02:17.643 --> 00:02:19.264
"That's tomorrow!"

47
00:02:19.284 --> 00:02:23.266
"But don't worry, we can do it," Maggie said quickly.

48
00:02:23.286 --> 00:02:26.007
"We've never failed to solve a case."

49
00:02:27.107 --> 00:02:28.788
There was a sudden shout from nearby.

50
00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:31.834
Henry saw a group of kids rushing toward them.

51
00:02:32.874 --> 00:02:35.416
Several of the kids were carrying baseball gloves or bats.

52
00:02:36.137 --> 00:02:37.658
All of them looked sweaty and tired.

53
00:02:37.678 --> 00:02:40.960
"Here come some customers," he told his friends.

54
00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.802
"They look thirsty."

55
00:02:42.822 --> 00:02:45.884
"Excuse us," Maggie told Mr.

56
00:02:45.924 --> 00:02:50.908
Tate. "As soon as we take care of these lemonade customers, we can talk more about your case."

57
00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.129
Mr. Tate checked his watch.

58
00:02:53.149 --> 00:02:56.752
"I'm meeting a plumber at the Dessert Den in a little while.

59
00:02:57.648 --> 00:03:00.509
There's a lot of last-minute work to do before the grand opening.

60
00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:03.711
Why don't you come over to the shop when you're finished here?"

61
00:03:06.232 --> 00:03:09.013
He hurried away before The Lemonade Detectives could answer.

62
00:03:10.013 --> 00:03:12.794
By then the baseball players had reached the lemonade stand.

63
00:03:13.755 --> 00:03:15.436
One of them was Henry's friend Nathan.

64
00:03:15.456 --> 00:03:18.617
"One lemonade, please," Nathan said.

65
00:03:19.597 --> 00:03:22.138
Henry and his friends poured lemonade for all the kids.

66
00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:27.989
Most of them left after they got their lemonade, but Nathan sat down on the grass to drink

67
00:03:28.029 --> 00:03:32.572
his. "We'd better get over to the Dessert Den," Cole told Henry and Maggie.

68
00:03:32.592 --> 00:03:35.933
"Mr. Tate needs us to solve this case fast."

69
00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:38.975
"We can't all go," Maggie said.

70
00:03:38.995 --> 00:03:42.177
"Somebody has to stay here to sell lemonade."

71
00:03:43.457 --> 00:03:44.658
"Okay," Cole said.

72
00:03:44.678 --> 00:03:47.680
"You stay here, and Henry and I will go talk to Mr.

73
00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.721
Tate." "No way!"

74
00:03:50.001 --> 00:03:50.841
Maggie complained.

75
00:03:50.861 --> 00:03:54.243
"I stayed while you two went to get ice cream, remember?

76
00:03:54.503 --> 00:03:55.784
It's somebody else's turn."

77
00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:57.809
She looked stubborn.

78
00:03:58.489 --> 00:03:59.250
So did Cole.

79
00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.251
Henry thought fast.

80
00:04:01.271 --> 00:04:03.872
"Hey, Nathan," he said.

81
00:04:03.892 --> 00:04:06.193
"Want to sell lemonade for us?

82
00:04:06.594 --> 00:04:08.195
You can keep half of our profits."

83
00:04:08.215 --> 00:04:10.796
"Sure!" Nathan said.

84
00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:13.338
"What?" Maggie squawked.

85
00:04:14.318 --> 00:04:15.139
Henry shrugged.

86
00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:19.921
"If you don't like my idea, you can stay instead," he told his cousin.

87
00:04:21.262 --> 00:04:22.183
Maggie scowled.

88
00:04:22.423 --> 00:04:24.284
But finally she agreed to the plan.

89
00:04:25.416 --> 00:04:27.598
"Let's take our bikes," Cole suggested.

90
00:04:27.618 --> 00:04:30.279
"West Belltown is pretty far away.

91
00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.581
It's too hot to walk there today."

92
00:04:38.805 --> 00:04:42.147
Once they reached West Belltown, they spotted the Dessert Den right away.

93
00:04:43.308 --> 00:04:45.830
It was the only finished building on the main avenue.

94
00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.173
The area around the Dessert Den was mostly covered in grass and weeds.

95
00:04:51.173 --> 00:04:53.835
Some kids were playing kickball in one of the grassy lots.

96
00:04:54.776 --> 00:04:57.313
"Look, there's my friend Emma," Maggie said.

97
00:04:58.054 --> 00:04:59.535
She waved and stopped her bike.

98
00:05:01.496 --> 00:05:03.098
Emma and the other kids hurried over.

99
00:05:05.439 --> 00:05:06.980
Henry knew all of them from school.

100
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.842
"What are you guys doing in West Belltown?"

101
00:05:10.283 --> 00:05:11.584
asked a kid named Robby.

102
00:05:12.624 --> 00:05:14.486
He was a year older than Henry and Cole.

103
00:05:14.506 --> 00:05:20.050
"The guy who owns the Dessert Den wants to hire us to solve a mystery," Maggie blurted out.

104
00:05:21.251 --> 00:05:22.952
Henry shot his cousin a warning look.

105
00:05:23.764 --> 00:05:26.767
Detectives had to be careful when they were talking about their cases.

106
00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:30.871
Robby's smile instantly turned into an angry scowl.

107
00:05:30.891 --> 00:05:32.913
"Why would you want to help him?

108
00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:34.555
Nobody wants him here!

109
00:05:35.516 --> 00:05:39.100
He should go back to wherever he came from and leave West Belltown alone!"
